# The building blocks for widgets installed from the store.
#
# A built-in view sits next to these files and writes `import ".."`. An
# installed one lives in its own folder under ~/.local/share and cannot, so it
# writes `import EdgeDash` instead. The window puts the qml directory on the
# import path, which is where Qt finds this file. Every entry points at the
# same file the built-in views use, so there is one Heading and not two.
module EdgeDash
Heading 1.0 ../Heading.qml
Chart 1.0 ../Chart.qml
CoreBars 1.0 ../CoreBars.qml
Confirm 1.0 ../Confirm.qml
MetricWidget 1.0 ../widgets/MetricWidget.qml
singleton Style 1.0 ../Style.qml
singleton Temperatures 1.0 ../widgets/Temperatures.qml
singleton Ui 1.0 ../Ui.qml
Glyph 1.0 ../Glyph.qml
Card 1.0 ../Card.qml
Chip 1.0 ../Chip.qml
IconButton 1.0 ../IconButton.qml
ActionButton 1.0 ../ActionButton.qml
Fab 1.0 ../Fab.qml
SectionHeader 1.0 ../SectionHeader.qml
Slider 1.0 ../Slider.qml
